      {id:"clients",title:"Associated states and clients",html:"<p>Local subsidiaries, joint ventures, banks, agents, and warehouses operate in China, Thailand, the Philippines, Indochina, and the archipelago. Governments can negotiate terms but rarely replace the complete network at once.</p>"},
      {id:"1985",title:"Mitsui in 1985",html:"<p>By 1985 Mitsui is an information, finance, logistics, and commodity empire. Its vulnerabilities are colonial debt, political backlash, opaque cross-guarantees, protected firms, and the need to preserve official favor.</p>"}
